{
  "name": "Annihilation Reactor",
  "icon": "theoreticalsciences:annihilation_reactor",
  "category": "theoreticalsciences:cosmic",
  "sortnum": 45,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:annihilation_reactor",
      "title": "Matter-Antimatter Annihilation Reactor",
      "text": "Day 12. Converts mass entirely into energy, E = mc^2, regulated by dilithium crystals. Nothing more efficient exists.$(br2)Generates power.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "When a particle meets its antiparticle, both vanish and all of their rest mass becomes energy - mostly gamma rays, via E = mc^2. Fission releases under 0.1% of the mass; annihilation releases 100%. One gram of antimatter matches dozens of kilotons of TNT."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Fuel log: it burns $(item)Antimatter Pellets$() (with a $(item)Dilithium Crystal$() as regulator) at 131,072 FE/t, or a full $(item)Annihilation Core$() at 524,288 FE/t.$(br2)It needs superfluid helium cooling. Do not skip this."
    },
